---

<BayPHL1 title="BayPHL 1: The Lost Books (Solution)">
  <Block>
    <a href="/1/"><strong>← Back to BayPHL 1</strong></a>
  </Block>

  <Block id="info">
    <h1 class="font-black font-roboto-slab text-4xl mb-4">
      The Lost Books (Solution)
    </h1>

    <p>
      (<a href={puzzle} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Puzzle</a>)
    </p>

    <p>
      The Lost Books is a puzzle about children’s books. In the puzzle, each
      image is the cover of a classic children’s book obscured using the <a
        href="https://github.com/fogleman/primitive">primitive</a
      > image processing library. The original title of each book has been replaced
      by an alternative title which (to help with identification) was somewhat thematic
      to the original book. (With “Bodywork” in particular, the reference was quite
      oblique — in the book, Madeline gets appendicitis and has to have her appendix
      removed).
    </p>

    <p>
      The new titles have the same number of words as the original titles, each
      with the same number of letters. However, in each pair of titles, only a
      single “<a
        href="https://www.puzzles.wiki/wiki/Eigenletters"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">eigenletter</a
      >“ is the same (from the flavortext, “only one small bit of each is still
      the same”). Reading those eigenletters in the order given yields the
      answer to the puzzle, <Answer>FRIENDLY PETER PAN</Answer>.
    </p>

    <table class="border-collapse mx-auto mb-4">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th class="text-center p-2">Puzzle</th>
          <th class="text-center p-2">Original</th>
          <th class="text-center p-2">Eigenletter</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          data.map(({ original, altered }) => {
            const cleanedAltered = altered.title
              .toUpperCase()
              .replaceAll(/[^A-Z ]/g, "");
            const cleanedOriginal = original.title
              .toUpperCase()
              .replaceAll(/[^A-Z ]/g, "");
            return (
              <tr>
                <td class="p-2 align-top">
                  <a
                    href={altered.img.src}
                    target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer"
                  >
                    <Image
                      class="max-w-60"
                      src={altered.img}
                      alt={altered.title}
                    />
                  </a>
                </td>
                <td class="p-2 align-top">
                  <a
                    href={original.img.src}
                    target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener noreferrer"
                  >
                    <Image
                      class="max-w-60"
                      src={original.img}
                      alt={original.title}
                    />
                  </a>
                  <td>
                    <div class="whitespace-nowrap font-roboto-mono">
                      {cleanedAltered}
                    </div>
                    <div class="whitespace-nowrap font-roboto-mono">
                      {cleanedOriginal}
                    </div>
                    <div class="whitespace-nowrap font-roboto-mono">
                      {cleanedAltered
                        .split("")
                        .map((c, i) =>
                          cleanedOriginal[i] === c ? (
                            <strong>{c}</strong>
                          ) : c === " " ? (
                            c
                          ) : (
                            "_"
                          )
                        )}
                    </div>
                  </td>
                </td>
              </tr>
            );
          })
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </Block>
</BayPHL1>
